<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Leopold, Prince of Anhalt-Köthen</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1694–1728</span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Leopold, Prince of Anhalt-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kothen">Köthen</a> from 1704 (ruling in person from 1715) to 1728, was a Calvinist ruler of a small German principality and a keen amateur musician. He is remembered for employing <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/johann-sebastian-bach">Johann Sebastian Bach</a> as his <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kapellmeister">Kapellmeister</a> from 1717 to 1723, when Bach composed much of his instrumental and chamber music, including works later gathered as the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brandenburg-concertos">Brandenburg Concertos</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/leopold-prince-of-anhalt-kothen.jpg" alt="Leopold, Prince of Anhalt-Köthen" width="320" height="454" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unidentified painter · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Leopold_von_Anhalt-K%C3%B6then_(1694_-_1728).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
